course: dictionary
lesson: 10831
title: Venomous: poison that bites and stings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Venomous» means able to put venom into you by biting or stinging. Venom is a kind of poison that gets into your body through a bite, a fang or a sting. The clue words «biting» and «stinging» show you how the poison gets in.
explain: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone and has venomous spines along its back, so reef shoes in shallow water protect your feet.» The spines are how the poison gets in, so venomous fits. The stonefish is hard to spot, which is why you need the shoes.
explain: The word can also describe words and looks. Venomous words or looks are full of hate and very unkind. If someone gives you a venomous look, swap in your meaning: "a very unkind, hateful look" still makes sense, so you know it is not about animals.
fact: «Venomous» means able to put venom into you by biting or stinging.
fact: Venom is a poison that goes into your body through a bite, a fang or a sting.
fact: «Venomous» can also describe words or looks that are full of hate and very unkind.
fact: The adder is the only venomous snake in Britain.
fact: The king cobra is the longest venomous snake, up to about 5 metres long.
exercise: «Lionfish have venomous spines and hunt small fish.» What does venomous mean here? | Fast and good at swimming | *Able to put venom in by stinging | Very bright and colourful | Hungry all the time
exercise: Which animal is the only venomous snake in Britain? | Slow worm | *Adder | Garden lizard | Grass snake
exercise: Jo says, «Her venomous look made me go quiet.» What does venomous mean here? | Bright and shiny | Friendly and warm | Able to sting | *Full of hate and very unkind
test: Which of these is the longest venomous snake? | Lionfish | *King cobra | Adder | Stonefish
test: Which phrase uses venomous to describe a look, not an animal? | venomous sting | venomous snake | venomous spines | *a venomous look
exam: If someone is bitten by a venomous snake in Australia, what should you do? | Suck the bite and cut it open quickly | Wait an hour to see what happens | *Call 000 and keep the person calm and still | Walk them quickly to the sea
